    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "85a22ac6_f3f9f46e",
        "filename": "zephyr/app/ec/usbc/svdm_rsp_dfp_only.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-23T03:40:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_... items are of limited scope, and aimed at identifying shimmed code (see zephyr/Kconfig)\nThere should be a corresponding CONFIG_USB_PD_XID that gets set in zephyr/shim/include/config_chip.h\nThis follows the consistent pattern and likely makes upstreaming easier.\nI think the plan was to avoid any reference to CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC.. defines in the legacy code, but I think some have snuck through.\n\nKeith may have some better context here.",
      "revId": "61ed2bf3ca44f567b67eaf67ab8ccbf04c2b9ffc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "98dc3a63_13197e8c",
        "filename": "zephyr/app/ec/usbc/svdm_rsp_dfp_only.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-23T17:29:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC is meant to create a distinct namespace from the legacy CONFIG_ options defined in platform/ec/include/config.h.\n\nThis CL creates new Kconfig options, and I agree that the support doesn\u0027t need to be added to the legacy cros-ec boards.\n\nI think dropping `PLATFORM_EC` from this name is appropriate for consistency with the other CONFIG_ options.",
      "parentUuid": "85a22ac6_f3f9f46e",
      "revId": "61ed2bf3ca44f567b67eaf67ab8ccbf04c2b9ffc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
